00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
 
the first special forces operation  detachment delta  or more commonly referred to as delta  force is an elite special mission unit  of the united states army the unit is  tasked with specialized missions  involving hostage rescue  and counter-terrorism as well as special  reconnaissance against high-value  targets  delta force is among the us military's  primary tier 1  special mission units tasked with  performing the most complex  classified and dangerous missions  delta force was formed after a number of  terrorist incidents that occurred during  the 1970s  although military and government  officials had been discussing this type  of unit since the early 60s  eventually it was agreed that the us  army needed units of highly adaptable  and completely autonomous teams who were  equipped with a wide range of skills for  direct action  and counter-terrorism missions delta  force was officially established  on the 19th of november 1977.  its primary goal is a counter-terrorist  unit specifically directed to kill  or capture high-value targets or  dismantle terrorist cells  but the unit is extremely flexible and  can also engage in direct action  missions  hostage rescues and covert assignments  the majority of operations assigned to  delta are classified  and most may never be known to the  public  applicants to delta force must be male  have at least two and a half years of  service  remaining in their enlistment be 21  years or older and score high enough  on the armed services vocational  aptitude battery a timed multi-aptitude  test  before they are able to attend the  initial briefing to even be considered  candidates must also be trained in  military parachuting and qualified to  participate  in airborne missions most importantly  they must be eligible for high-level  security clearance  and have not been convicted by  court-martial or have any disciplinary  action noted in their official military  personnel file  the following selection would often only  see 10 to 12 percent of applicants  completing the course after the  reactivation of team rainbow in 2015  one delta force operator was recruited  to bring their skills and expertise to  assist in the fight against terrorism  on a global scale this operator was  named  [Music]  [Music]  maverick  i was trapped for a long time  lived and seen things you couldn't  imagine  now i see things in a different light  here thorne code named maverick is an  attacking operator  in team rainbow maverick grew up in  boston massachusetts  and was part of a multilingual family  his parents were kind and loving but  they were often very strict  and decidably inflexible when it came to  presenting him with the outside  experiences away from the family  a naturally gifted child his parents  pushed him to be better  to aim higher and provided him with an  almost overwhelming magnitude of  different sensory experiences  that most kids his own age would have  struggled with  it's fair to say that he thrived in this  type of environment through being able  to break things down around him and  group them into manageable chunks  he was able to thrive and grow at a pace  that left the other kids behind  this resulted in maturity and growth  beyond his years and this was shown in  intelligence tests  scoring highly and in the top two  percent among kids his own age  after high school he enlisted with the  us army and quickly rose through the  ranks  although he was exposed to a number of  experiences at home he had very few  opportunities to explore outside of his  own backyard  and this is one of the driving factors  that led him to join the army  where he could experience the world in a  way he was unable to growing up he  learned dari and became an intelligence  officer  serving in kabul the capital of  afghanistan and it was during this time  that a number of foreign reporters  tourists and criminals were also  flocking into the city  maverick was well known in the  underground club scene and especially  among the locals as a proficient ukashi  player  which is a central asian sport where  horse-mounted players attempt to place a  goat  or calf carcass in a goal  eventually maverick was invited into  delta force as a regional specialist  his role was to remain in the country  gathering intel building networks  establishing safe houses and tracking  hostiles  but as the situation in afghanistan  started to deteriorate  a lot of his time was spent keeping an  eye on americans and helping the locals  to escape the growing violence  even right from the start merrick knew  that the period of peace would  eventually end  he could see the injection of people  coming from outside the country  especially westerners  flooding in drinking at restaurants and  partying in the underground clubs  he saw what was coming long before  anyone else  insurgent groups could see that the  westerners were easy targets in these  situations  it was only a matter of time before they  acted on it  and then somewhere along the way while  maverick was investigating a missing  reporter  delta force completely lost contact with  him  two years pass before he is seen again  unexpectedly  he was discovered by specialist knock  and with him he had enough intel to  dismantle a major insurgency operation  working in the area  understandably there was still a number  of questions floating around about his  abrupt disappearance  but regardless he was exonerated and his  evidence sealed  it was the success of missions like  these that first gained in the attention  of six a legend among intelligence  operatives  maverick is known as the agent who went  native  his intellect an intimidating level of  skill when it comes to reading others  make him somewhat difficult person to  interact with however  bringing up kabul or buskashi will  quickly bring him out of his shell  on the other hand maverick is  exceptionally empathetic that comes from  his strong  ability to watch listen and dissect  situations  people often openly confide in them  which is a skill that likely assisted  him in his survival while operating in  kabul  information around maverick's  disappearance tells the story of a  horrific ordeal  but the experience and the scars that  came with it only brought him closer to  afghanistan  he has a tattoo on his left arm as a  reminder of the time he spent there  although maverick's mind and body is  with team rainbow his heart is very  obviously still in kabul  maverick's gadget is a diy blue torch  called suri  siri can breach any surface including  reinforced walls and hatches  though it requires a steady hand in a  knowledge of the environment to create  small holes and lines of sight  the torch makes almost no sound but will  rapidly deplete fuel supplies  regardless the high precision of this  tool makes it useful in a variety of  situations  without relying on digital technology  i love seeing these backstories with the  other operators crossover  i'm actually thinking of putting  together a video on the relationships  between each specialist  it could be interesting and probably  super difficult to follow  i'll think about it for now i think i'm  going to go see if there are any local  new zealand buskashi clubs around  i'm very intrigued by this sport  otherwise thank you very much for  watching i hope you've enjoyed it  and i'll catch you in the next one  cheers  so  you

